-- title:
--   Supersingular chart point yields supersingular place of level-M fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K_2$ be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 (M * p)))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the subfield of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by ratios of $q$-expansions of integral modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_0(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K_2$, let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $j_2\in K_2$ be nonzero with underlying Laurent series the image of $j_q$ under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Write $A_2=$ `chartAlgFin A K₂ j₂` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K_2$ of elements integral over $A[j_2]$, and let $y_2$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_2$ such that, for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon A_2\to\Omega$ with kernel the prime $\mathfrak{y}_2$ of $y_2$, the image $\varphi(j_2)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has trivial $p$-torsion; assume moreover that $\varpi$ maps into $\mathfrak{y}_2$. Let $e\colon L\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be a ring homomorphism and $A^\flat$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with algebraically closed residue field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, such that $e$ carries $A$ into $A^\flat$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ exactly when $e(a)$ lies in that of $A^\flat$. Finally let `data` be a modular polynomial datum for $p$ (a monic $\Phi$ of degree $\psi(p)$ in two variables vanishing on $(j_q,j_q^{(p)})$) satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi\equiv (Y^p-X)(Y-X^p) \bmod p$, let the two Hecke degeneracy embeddings at level $(M,p)$ be integral, and let $P$ be a place specialisation over $A^\flat$ with residue map $A^\flat\to\kappa$, together with a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Then there are a place $w$ of [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldC κ M`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L61) lying in [`ModularCurve.ssPlaces p M κ`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularNodePlaces.html#L113) — so $w$ is rational, is an affine geometric place, and its value at `jGeomGen κ M` is a supersingular $j$-invariant — and a ring homomorphism $\rho\colon A_2\to$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ M` such that: for each $b\in A_2$ there is $f$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar (M * p)`, integral for $R.R_1$, whose Laurent series is the image of that of $b$ under the coefficient map induced by $e$, with $\rho(b)$ the value of `R.residue₁` at $f$; $\rho(\varpi)=0$; $\rho(j_2)=$ `jGeomGen κ M`; $\rho$ takes values in the valuation subring of $w$; $\rho(b)$ is a nonunit there precisely when $b\in\mathfrak{y}_2$; and every element of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M` is a ratio $a/b$ with $a,b$ in the $\kappa$-subalgebra generated by the image of $\rho$ and $b\neq 0$.
--
--   This is the point-to-place dictionary at a supersingular closed point of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model of $X_0(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring containing $\zeta_p$: the point $\mathfrak{y}_2$ of the special fibre is matched with a supersingular place of the function field of the level-$M$ curve over $\kappa$, read through the first residue map of the prolongation tuple, in accordance with the description of $X_0(Mp)$ in characteristic $p$ as two copies of $X_0(M)$ crossing at the supersingular points. It feeds the subsequent identification of the completed local ring at such a point with the stalk of a crossing model.
